<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving logarithmic equation by quotient rule</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the equation</p>
\[ \log_{{@a@}} ({@b*x+1@}) - \log_{{@a@}} ({@x-c@}) = 1. \]
<p>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>Use the quotient law to write the left-hand side as one logarithm:</p>
\[ \log_{{@a@}} \left(\frac{{@b*x+1@}}{{@x-c@}}\right) = 1. \]
<p>In index form, the number inside equals \({@a@}^1 = {@a@}\):</p>
\[ \frac{{@b*x+1@}}{{@x-c@}} = {@a@} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad {@b*x+1@} = {@a@}({@x-c@}) = {@a*x-a*c@}. \]
\[ {@a*c@} + 1 = {@a*x@} - {@b*x@} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x = {@ta1@}. \]
<p>Check: \(x - {@c@} = {@ta1-c@} > 0\) and \({@b*x@} + 1 > 0\), so both logarithms are defined.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
